PART 17 – Git Branching Cheat Sheet

Ask students to maintain this command reference.

| Command | Purpose |
| `git branch` | List branches |
| `git branch feature` | Create branch |
| `git switch feature` | Switch branch |
| `git switch -c feature` | Create and switch |
| `git branch -m new-name` | Rename current branch |
| `git branch -d feature` | Delete merged branch |
| `git branch -D feature` | Force-delete branch |
| `git branch -a` | List all branches |
| `git merge feature` | Merge feature into current branch |
| `git merge --abort` | Abort an in-progress merge |
| `git log --graph --oneline --all` | Visualize commit history |
| `git rebase main` | Rebase current branch onto main |
| `git rebase --continue` | Continue rebase |
| `git rebase --abort` | Abort rebase |
| `git switch main` | Switch to main |
| `git checkout <commit>` | Check out a specific commit |

